// The app's features — one line each: FEATURE(<component>), whose namespace of the same name defines Install().
//
// This line is the feature's whole wiring. main/CMakeLists.txt makes the component a requirement of main, and
// main.cpp calls <component>::Install() after app_shell::Install() and before app_shell::Run(). Install() registers
// what the feature does with app_hooks; the shell names no feature. Deleting the line removes the feature, and
// MINIMAL_BUILD then builds nothing only it required (APP_ARCHITECTURE §1, §4).
//
// Only lines starting FEATURE( are read, by the preprocessor and by CMake alike.
FEATURE(hello)
